# Stub rules for github.com/danielgtaylor/huma/v2 (v2.37.2, checked against the
# module cache at /root/.local/share/go/pkg/mod/github.com/danielgtaylor/huma/v2@v2.37.2).
#
# Every rule's file:line is in its comment. Judgment calls are explained below.
#
# 1. huma.NewError is a package-level VARIABLE of func type (error.go:231, "var
#    NewError = func(status int, msg string, errs ...error) StatusError"). A call
#    to it is a dynamic call. Its default implementation only reads its arguments
#    and builds an *ErrorModel (error.go:231-250), so the effects rule is pure.
#    Caveat: an application may replace the variable at start-up (error.go:224
#    documents "huma.NewError = func(...)"). The rules describe the default.
#
# 2. Status-carrying constructors. Each Error<NNN><Name> (error.go:281-477) is
#    "return NewError(http.Status<Name>, msg, errs...)", so the error it returns
#    carries the status in its name. The rule says so for errset: the call
#    returns a carried variant with that status (see errset/carried.go). The 40
#    lines were generated from the source and each code was checked against the
#    http.Status<Name> constant in the body of the function.
#
# 3. NewError and NewErrorWithContext take the status as an argument: "arg:N"
#    names the argument index (NewError: 0, error.go:231; NewErrorWithContext:
#    1, after the Context at 0, error.go:251). A non-constant status is unknown.
#
# 4. Route registration (huma.go:2281-2383 for Get/Post/Put/Patch/Delete, and
#    huma.go:708 for Register). Get/Post/Put/Patch/Delete take the path at index 1
#    and the handler at index 2. Register takes an huma.Operation as argument 1,
#    so its method and path are the Method and Path fields of that composite
#    literal (@1.Method, @1.Path).
#
# 5. The default errmap: huma sends an error that implements StatusError with
#    the status it reports (huma.go:1096-1106: errors.As(err, &StatusError) ->
#    GetStatus()), and every other error as 500 "unexpected error occurred".
#    errors.As also finds a %w-wrapped StatusError. errset cannot read GetStatus
#    of an arbitrary type, so a non-carried StatusError has an unknown status.

effects github.com/danielgtaylor/huma/v2.NewError pure

status github.com/danielgtaylor/huma/v2.Error400BadRequest 400   # error.go:281-282
status github.com/danielgtaylor/huma/v2.Error401Unauthorized 401   # error.go:286-287
status github.com/danielgtaylor/huma/v2.Error402PaymentRequired 402   # error.go:291-292
